1
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:08,680
decoration, the Order of the Green Banner, which he had conferred upon himself.

2
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:15,559
In the general rejoicings, the unfortunate affair of the banknotes was forgotten.

3
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:19,920
It was a few days later than this that the pigs came upon a case of whiskey in

4
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:22,280
the cellars of the farmhouse.

5
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:26,360
It had been overlooked at the time when the house was first occupied.

6
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:31,479
That night, there came from the farmhouse the sound of loud singing, in

7
00:00:31,479 --> 00:00:38,360
which, to everyone's surprise, the strains of Beasts of England were mixed up.

8
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:42,719
At about half past nine, Napoleon, wearing an old bowler hat of Mr.

9
00:00:42,719 --> 00:00:47,079
Jones's, was distinctly

10
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:55,680
seen to emerge from the back door, gallop rapidly round the yard, and disappear indoors again.

11
00:00:55,680 --> 00:01:00,959
But in the morning, a deep silence hung over the farmhouse.

12
00:01:00,959 --> 00:01:04,639
Not a pig appeared to be stirring.

13
00:01:04,639 --> 00:01:09,559
It was nearly nine o'clock when Squealer made his appearance, walking slowly and

14
00:01:09,559 --> 00:01:15,360
dejectedly, his eyes dull, his tail hanging limply behind him,

15
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:19,799
and with every appearance of being seriously ill.

16
00:01:19,799 --> 00:01:26,040
He called the animals together and told them that he had a terrible piece of news to impart.

17
00:01:26,040 --> 00:01:29,319
Comrade Napoleon was dying.

18
00:01:29,319 --> 00:01:32,000
A cry of lamentation went up.

19
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:38,280
Straw was laid down outside the doors of the farmhouse, and the animals walked on tiptoe.

20
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:42,479
With tears in their eyes, they asked one another what they should do if their

21
00:01:42,479 --> 00:01:45,159
leader were taken away from them.

22
00:01:45,159 --> 00:01:50,879
A rumor went round that Snowball had, after all, contrived to introduce poison

23
00:01:50,879 --> 00:01:53,440
into Napoleon's food.

24
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:57,920
At 11 o'clock, Squealer came out to make another announcement.

25
00:01:57,920 --> 00:02:04,079
As his last act upon Earth, Comrade Napoleon had pronounced a solemn decree.

26
00:02:04,079 --> 00:02:08,639
The drinking of alcohol was to be punished by death.

27
00:02:08,639 --> 00:02:13,159
By the evening, however, Napoleon appeared to be somewhat better, and the

28
00:02:13,159 --> 00:02:18,959
following morning Squealer was able to tell them that he was well on the way to recovery.

29
00:02:18,959 --> 00:02:23,719
By the evening of that day, Napoleon was back at work, and on the next day it was

30
00:02:23,719 --> 00:02:28,719
learned that he had instructed Whymper to purchase in Willingdon some booklets

31
00:02:28,719 --> 00:02:31,479
on brewing and distilling.

32
00:02:31,479 --> 00:02:36,280
A week later, Napoleon gave orders that the small paddock beyond the orchard,

33
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:40,399
which it had previously been intended to set aside as a grazing ground for

34
00:02:40,399 --> 00:02:44,639
animals who were past work, was to be plowed up.

35
00:02:44,639 --> 00:02:49,639
It was given out that the pasture was exhausted and needed reseeding,

36
00:02:49,639 --> 00:02:55,040
but it soon became known that Napoleon intended to sow it with barley.

37
00:02:55,040 --> 00:03:01,840
About this time, there occurred a strange incident which hardly anyone was able to understand.

38
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:07,920
One night, at about 12:00, there was a loud crash in the yard, and the animals

39
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:10,559
rushed out of their stalls.

40
00:03:10,559 --> 00:03:13,079
It was a moonlit night.

41
00:03:13,079 --> 00:03:17,120
At the foot of the end wall of the big barn, where the Seven Commandments were

42
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:21,719
written, there lay a ladder broken in two pieces.

43
00:03:21,719 --> 00:03:27,399
Squealer, temporarily stunned, was sprawling beside it, and near at hand,

44
00:03:27,399 --> 00:03:33,239
there lay a lantern, a paintbrush, and an overturned pot of white paint.

45
00:03:33,239 --> 00:03:37,639
The dogs immediately made a ring round Squealer and escorted him back to the

46
00:03:37,639 --> 00:03:41,159
farmhouse as soon as he was able to walk.

47
00:03:41,159 --> 00:03:45,920
None of the animals could form any idea as to what this meant, except old

48
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:51,280
Benjamin, who nodded his muzzle with a knowing air and seemed to understand,

49
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:53,000
but would say nothing.
